{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "Living the Dream", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "The Opportunity to Win an Offer", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 9, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 16, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.1", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Describe hypothetical situations in written and spoken interactions according to work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Understands specific information in written texts ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.  Understands specific information in written texts ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Understands specific information in written texts ", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "engenn9le16ob09re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": " Talking Hypothetically About the Past", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " When you want to talk about situations in the past in a hypothetical context (not real or necessarily true), you can use the structures <span class=\"italic\">would have</span>, <span class=\"italic\">should have</span> and <span class=\"italic\">could have</span>.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Could have </span> (+ past participle) means that it was possible to do something at a time in the past, or you had the ability to do something, however, you did not do it.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">could have called</span>, but I thought it was too late.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You also use <span class=\"italic\">could have </span> to make a guess about something that happened in the past.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Where is Denise?</span><br/> <span class=\"italic\">She <span class=\"strong\">could have been </span> delayed downtown  or she <span class=\"strong\">could have overslept</span>.</span> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Should have</span> (+ past participle) means that you had some obligation to do something in the past, or that it may have been a good idea to do something, however, you did not do it.<span class=\"italic\"> Should have</span> can express regret about something you did or did not do.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">should have prepared more</span>. </span> (I regret not preparing.)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">She <span class=\"strong\">should have answered </span> that question differently. </span> (She didn't answer that question very well and she should have done it differently.)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">would have</span> ( + past participle) to refer to something you wanted to do in the past, but didn't do. This is like the third conditional, but an \u2018if-clause' is not used.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">would have called </span> and invited you, but I didn't know your phone number.</span> <br/> (I wanted to call you but I didn't know your number, so I didn't phone you.)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I could have come over after nine, but I thought it was too late. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I should have called earlier in the day. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I  thought she should have said this and she could have answered that. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "She should have been much more formal and she shouldn't have talked so much.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "She could have just responded with, \u201cFine, thank you\u201d or she could have asked the interviewer how he was. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": " Well, that should have made you feel quite confident.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": " The Future", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You can use four different tenses to talk about the future.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When you talk about things that are not decided or when you make a decision at the moment of speaking for the future, you use the modal <span class=\"italic\">will</span>. <br> For example: <br> <span class=\"italic\">Well, they will contact me before 3:00 p.m. Friday.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you ask about intentions, you use <span class=\"italic\">be going to</span>. <br> For example: <br> <span class=\"italic\">Based on my interview, I think I'm going to get this job!</span> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you talk about things that are arranged, on the agenda or booked for the future, you use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Continuous </span>tense. <br> For example: <br> <span class=\"italic\">Are you going to send a thank you e-mail?</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you talk about schedules, you use the <span class=\"strong\">Simple Present</span>. <br> For example: <br> <span class=\"italic\">We leave at 5 tonight. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Well, they will contact me before 3:00 p.m. Friday.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Are you going to send a thank you e-mail?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I will do that after we leave.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I'm also madly researching BFP for any other information on the web.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Based on my interview, I think I'm going to get this job! ", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to hit it out of the park", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to do extremely well", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I think I hit it out of the park! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le16ob09aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": " These are words you hear when someone feels confident!", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to critique", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to analyze", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I sat there and critiqued this person's interview. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le16ob09aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "right out of the gate", "type": "name"}, {"content": "from the beginning ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I think it turned the interviewer off right out of the gate.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le16ob09aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "concisely", "type": "name"}, {"content": " in few words", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I answered all his questions clearly and concisely.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le16ob09aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "madly", "type": "name"}, {"content": "as fast as possible; quickly ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm also madly researching BFP for any other information on the web.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le16ob09aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Watch YouTube videos about bad job interviews.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "With a partner, make a list of all the faults you see.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write sentences using <span class=\"italic\">could have</span>, <span class=\"italic\">would have</span>, and <span class=\"italic\">should have</span> to explain what you would have done differently.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Present your video and report what you would have hypothetically changed to the rest of the class.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I watch a mock job interview and break down the faults in it. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I make sentences using <span class=\"italic\">could have</span>,<span class=\"italic\"> should have</span>, and <span class=\"italic\">would have</span> to explain what I would change.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I present my video and share my ideas with the rest of the class.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "contents": [{}], "_data": [], "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"image": "engenn9le16ob09re2img05.jpg", "time": "0", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"image": "engenn9le16ob09re2img05.jpg", "time": "100", "id": 1, "text": "<span class= \"strong\"> Bianca</span>: Sorry, I was super busy the other day. I could have come over after nine, but I thought it was too late. I should have called earlier in the day.<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Kristi</span>: It's ok.<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Bianca</span>: So how did the interview go?<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Kristi</span>: It went really well. I think I hit it out of the park!<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Bianca</span>: Fantastic! You didn't get nervous?<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Kristi</span>:  Nope. I was well prepared and was able to answer all his questions clearly and concisely and I had a secret weapon.<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Bianca</span>: What was that?<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Kristi</span>: Well, I got there early and I sat right next to the interview room door ... and I could hear everything.<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Bianca</span>: Wow!<br />"}, {"image": "engenn9le16ob09re2img07.jpg", "time": "54000", "id": 2, "text": "<span class= \"strong\"> Kristi:</span> I listened to another candidate being interviewed.<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Bianca</span>: Did it help?<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Kristi</span>: It helped me so much! I sat there and critiqued that person's interview. I  thought she should have said this and  she could have answered that.<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Bianca</span>: Oh yeah? Give me an example.<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Kristi</span>: Well, this woman responded to a basic polite greeting in an extremely informal manner.<br />\nShe should have been much more formal and she shouldn't have talked so much.<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Bianca</span>: What did she say?<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Kristi</span>: She answered a simple how are you question with her life story. She could have just responded with, \u201cFine thank you\u201d or she could have asked the interviewer how he was.  I think it turned the interviewer off right out of the gate.<br />"}, {"image": "engenn9le16ob09re2img06.jpg", "time": "104000", "id": 3, "text": "<span class= \"strong\"> Bianca</span>: Well, that should have made you feel quite confident.<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Kristi</span>: Extremely!<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Bianca</span>: So what's the next step in the interview process?<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Kristi</span>: Well, they will contact me before 3:00 p.m. Friday.<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Bianca</span>: Are you going to send a thank you e-mail?<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Kristi</span>: I will do that after we leave. I'm also madly researching BFP for any other information on the web. Based on my interview, I think I'm going to get this job!<br />"}], "audiosrc": "engenn9le16ob09re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn9le16ob09re2img05.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "id": 1}], "exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": " I can talk about events and experiences related to jobs.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can discuss hypothetical situations in the past.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can participate in interviews.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " What are some movies that you think could have been really good if only they were done differently?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": "What would you change about them?", "type": "Free Header Item"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "allowed_attempts": 2}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "I wouldn't have done it like that!", "type": "free_ty